"""Batch 02: speed, priority and KO races (about 60%), plus hard mixes of items, abilities, status and doubles.

Every claim that depends on an item, an ability, the weather, a status or the turn order goes through the ops in
tests/ai_checks.py: mfaster / first for who moves (Choice Scarf, paralysis under both rules, Quick Feet, Sand Rush,
Lagging Tail, trained Speed, levels, priority brackets), mko / mnoko for the hits, race / loses / setup_wins for fights
counted over two or three turns (a Sitrus Berry, a priority move, Dragon Dance), chip_kos for a poison or weather tick
that finishes a Pokémon, and status_only / no_endure / survives_recoil / macc / fixed_ko for the rules a key rests on
(accuracy under No Guard and Hustle, Seismic Toss, Focus Punch, Sucker Punch, Rock Head). Variable-power moves whose
power follows the Speeds, the HP, a status or an item (Gyro Ball, Electro Ball, Reversal, Brine, Hex, Acrobatics) are
checked by the same damage ops. A built-in op appears next to them where it shows the contrast (a plain `faster` the
Scarf, a paralysis or an ability overturns).

The first twenty scenarios and the thirty after them were written by two authors in turn; the ids are all b02_.
"""
